  "note": "Verso body page, TWO columns in the top third only: Figure 1.26 and its cyan caption sit in the wide OUTER (left) margin column x 0.129-0.411, with blocks 1 and 3-6 set in a narrow measure beside them, x 0.442-0.903; a clean empty gutter separates them at x 0.411-0.442. From block 7 (y 0.325) the text reverts to the single full measure x 0.314-0.903, which spans both declared columns, so those elements are column 'full'. The boundary was set by measuring the left edge each element is actually set to rather than by where the figure stops: block 6's equation is still indented to x 0.474 like the other narrow-measure equations (blocks 1 and 4), not to x 0.374 like the full-measure equation (block 13), so it is column 'right' even though the margin column beside it is already empty. Elements are in A2's block order, which is the reading order. The figure caption has no A2 block and takes n: null; it is printed entirely in the chapter cyan #00adef. No fill is reported for the figure - the blue of the cylinder is artwork, not a panel tint. Blocks 9 and 10, the italic statement of Gauss's law and its 'q = ...' gloss, are reported as role paragraph with font serif-italic, which is how they are set; block 9 carries the equation number (1.31) flush right at x 0.900. page_header_band is the pale blue #c6eafb strip across the whole page top (y 0-0.067); its #41c7f4 hairline and #00adef foot rule are internal edges of that one band, so no rule_bar is reported, and this page has no footer_rule of any kind. The '2022-23' edition line at the foot is recorded as a second running_header because the allowed role list has no footer-text role. All 16 A2 blocks matched by position."
